{"title":"Systems Programmer Roadmap","role":"Systems Programmer","summary":"A Systems Programmer develops and maintains software that operates close to the computer's hardware and operating system. The role focuses on operating systems, system utilities, low-level programming, memory, processes, networking, compilers, device interaction, and performance optimization.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Computer Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Systems Programmer develops and maintains software that operates close to the computer's hardware and operating system. The role focuses on operating systems, system utilities, low-level programming, memory, processes, networking, compilers, device interaction, and performance optimization."},{"type":"p","text":"Compared with a general application developer, a Systems Programmer works much closer to the underlying computing platform."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical Responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Develop system-level software"},{"text":"Work with operating-system components"},{"text":"Develop system utilities and services"},{"text":"Write efficient C/C++/Rust code"},{"text":"Work with processes and threads"},{"text":"Manage memory and system resources"},{"text":"Develop drivers or low-level components"},{"text":"Debug crashes and performance issues"},{"text":"Work with Linux/Unix environments"},{"text":"Optimize CPU, memory and I/O usage"},{"text":"Build networking and infrastructure software"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Direction","Example Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Systems Programming"},{"text":"Systems Programmer, Systems Software Engineer"}],[{"text":"Operating Systems"},{"text":"OS Engineer, Kernel Engineer"}],[{"text":"Infrastructure"},{"text":"Infrastructure Software Engineer"}],[{"text":"Embedded Systems"},{"text":